<title>UK: ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</title>
<headline>ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said the 4,250 tonne buffer-stock sale earlier on Thursday was completed at the following prices.</p>
<p>ORIGIN	  TONNES  CROP YEAR	QUALITY   U.S. DOLLAR/TONNE</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   217   1981/82-82/83    GF	$1,354-1,365</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire 1,258   1987/88	    GF	$1,403-1,408</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   301   1987/88	    FF	$1,325</p>
<p>Ghana	     600   1987/88	    GF	$1,408-1,417</p>
<p>Ghana	     591   1987/88	    FF	$1,370-1,387</p>
<p>Nigeria	   248   1986/87	    GF	$1,384</p>
<p>Nigeria	   207   1986/87	    FF	$1,300</p>
<p>Togo		 25   1987/88	    GF	$1,403</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   526   1981/82	   FAQ	$1,270-1,301</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   197   1982/83	   FAQ	$1,290-1,293</p>
<p>Nigeria	    81   1986/87	   FAQ	$1,270</p>
<p>(GF=good fermented, FF=fair fermented, FAQ= fair to average quality)</p>
<p>The ICCO said the carry for forward delivery was calculated at $12 per tonne per month.</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom 44 171 542 8072.</p>
</text>
